@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0
// Astral Chain v1.0.1, applied after Dynamic-FPS 1.0.1.pchtxt (native_trace --patch, in that order).
//
// Cutscenes: Dynamic-FPS's measured step at 60 FPS, with a larger step limit (8 ticks instead of 2) so a cutscene
// catches up after a stall of up to ~270 ms instead of falling behind its audio. Measured on the opening cutscene by
// matching picture content against the unmodified game (30 FPS, fixed step): the time between points 42-90 s apart was
// the same to within 0.1 s, i.e. no drift.
//
// AC_CUTSCENE_FPS=30 plays cutscenes as the unmodified game does instead: its own fixed-step path (main+0x91DC48,
// step 1.0, whole extra frames after a stall) at a steady 30 FPS (nvn_hle.h nvn_present_pace).
//
// The step code reports cutscene mode to the runtime every frame (svc #0xB1, host_runtime.c.in); the runtime returns
// the mode in w21 (the function restores x21 on return). The game's cutscene mode is timer flag bit 30 (w21 == 0).
//
// 0xA0E7F8 held "fmov s1,#2" (the maximum step) in the mod's code cave; it branches to 8 new words after the cave's
// last one (0xA0EFD0), still inside the executable page that ends the text segment.

@flag offset_shift 0x100

@enabled
00A0E7F8 F7010014 // b 0xA0EFD4
00A0EFD4 211600D4 // svc #0xB1: cutscene mode to the runtime (w21: 1 gameplay, 0 cutscene, 2 cutscene at 30 FPS)
00A0EFD8 0110201E // fmov s1,#2.0: gameplay maximum step
00A0EFDC B5000037 // tbnz w21,#0,0xA0EFF0: gameplay
00A0EFE0 75000837 // tbnz w21,#1,0xA0EFEC: cutscene at 30 FPS
00A0EFE4 0110241E // fmov s1,#8.0: cutscene maximum step (catch-up after a stall)
00A0EFE8 02000014 // b 0xA0EFF0
00A0EFEC 173BFC17 // b 0x91DC48: the original's fixed-step path (str s8,[x19,#0xD0])
00A0EFF0 03FEFF17 // b 0xA0E7FC: fminnm s0,s0,s1
@stop
